WEBVTT

00:00:09.370 --> 00:00:11.830
I'll do it.

00:00:11.830 --> 00:00:15.410
Will you let me fix Miss Fujito's dress,

00:00:15.410 --> 00:00:16.790
Mr. Yanagida?!

00:00:40.120 --> 00:00:43.290
"Smile Down the Runway"

00:01:52.620 --> 00:01:55.000
"Episode 3"
"Smile Down the Runway"
What could you possibly do, Bob?

00:01:55.000 --> 00:01:55.750
--Huh...? What's happening?

00:01:55.750 --> 00:01:56.620
--I don't know. But I'm just going to do it!
--Huh...? What's happening?

00:01:56.620 --> 00:01:58.540
--I don't know. But I'm just going to do it!
--That boy's saying he'll fix the dress.

00:01:58.540 --> 00:02:00.200
Does he even know how to sew?

00:02:00.200 --> 00:02:03.120
Mr. Yanagida! We're out of time!

00:02:03.120 --> 00:02:04.330
All right.

00:02:04.330 --> 00:02:06.120
I'll guide you through this.

00:02:06.120 --> 00:02:07.450
Just do exactly what I say.

00:02:07.450 --> 00:02:08.580
No!

00:02:08.580 --> 00:02:11.450
The 40 dresses are all out of order!

00:02:11.450 --> 00:02:14.160
We can't do this without you directing us!

00:02:14.160 --> 00:02:15.330
Damn it.

00:02:16.160 --> 00:02:18.540
You'll find him intriguing. Trust me.

00:02:19.660 --> 00:02:23.620
Sure, he is a bit rough around the edges,

00:02:23.620 --> 00:02:27.910
but within his head, the designs
are completely thought out.

00:02:28.950 --> 00:02:31.750
You of all people should know

00:02:31.750 --> 00:02:33.540
how difficult that is...

00:02:35.040 --> 00:02:37.330
Hey, Bob!

00:02:37.330 --> 00:02:41.370
Just don't forget
what this brand is about, got it?

00:02:41.370 --> 00:02:42.370
Yes!

00:02:43.660 --> 00:02:45.290
I'm sorry to keep you wait--

00:02:45.290 --> 00:02:48.160
Still doing makeup. I'll finish soon!

00:02:50.120 --> 00:02:51.540
"Doom"

00:02:51.540 --> 00:02:53.580
"Doom"
I-I'll do my best.

00:02:55.160 --> 00:02:56.250
I got this.

00:02:56.250 --> 00:02:59.830
Mr. Yanagida's brand concept is to
make clothes for independent women

00:02:59.830 --> 00:03:02.160
that are as strong as they are.

00:03:02.160 --> 00:03:06.790
I need to maintain that image
and fit it to Miss Fujito's size...

00:03:06.790 --> 00:03:10.040
Think... Think... Think...

00:03:14.870 --> 00:03:19.040
F-First, I need to do something
about this hem touching the floor...

00:03:20.290 --> 00:03:22.790
Hey, are you sure about cutting that hem?

00:03:22.790 --> 00:03:25.160
Huh? What do you mean...?

00:03:25.160 --> 00:03:28.790
Miss Moriyama specifically said
she couldn't cut the hem...

00:03:29.870 --> 00:03:33.000
Right, it'd be too much of a hassle.

00:03:33.000 --> 00:03:36.790
I'll have to prevent the fabric from fraying...

00:03:36.790 --> 00:03:40.410
Thick fabric takes more time to alter...

00:03:40.410 --> 00:03:42.870
There's no time to do it by hand...

00:03:42.870 --> 00:03:44.540
Then...

00:03:44.540 --> 00:03:46.160
Should I use a sewing machine?

00:03:46.160 --> 00:03:48.410
I've never used this type before...

00:03:48.410 --> 00:03:50.410
But I've got no choice!

00:03:50.410 --> 00:03:51.370
Miss Fujito!

00:03:51.370 --> 00:03:53.000
Please undress for me.

00:03:53.000 --> 00:03:55.290
Okay! I need the fitter!

00:03:58.160 --> 00:04:01.290
I don't have a thick enough needle
for this fabric...

00:04:01.290 --> 00:04:03.000
I need durability.

00:04:03.000 --> 00:04:04.540
Do I use a thin needle?

00:04:04.540 --> 00:04:08.120
Unwieldy fabric and
an unfamiliar sewing machine...

00:04:08.120 --> 00:04:10.370
If the needle gives out on me...

00:04:10.370 --> 00:04:11.370
...I'm screwed!

00:04:12.750 --> 00:04:15.040
I'm going to go draw up a design...

00:04:15.040 --> 00:04:15.910
What?

00:04:15.910 --> 00:04:17.410
Hey! There's no time...!

00:04:17.410 --> 00:04:19.660
I know!

00:04:19.660 --> 00:04:21.200
Tsumura...

00:04:23.700 --> 00:04:26.500
I need to figure out another way...

00:04:26.500 --> 00:04:28.830
There's more to fix than just the hem.

00:04:28.830 --> 00:04:31.580
The dress is too big overall.

00:04:31.580 --> 00:04:34.000
And most importantly...

00:04:34.000 --> 00:04:36.870
...the dress must live up to the Yanagida name!

00:04:40.620 --> 00:04:42.660
Hey, is he okay?

00:04:42.660 --> 00:04:44.370
He doesn't seem okay...

00:04:44.370 --> 00:04:46.120
How much time do we have?

00:04:46.120 --> 00:04:47.910
Less than a minute.

00:04:47.910 --> 00:04:50.620
He's not going to make it...

00:04:52.080 --> 00:04:53.750
Oh, no...

00:04:53.750 --> 00:04:56.540
Mr. Yanagida! This isn't good...

00:04:56.540 --> 00:05:00.750
We could use the tallest woman
on the staff as a replacement model.

00:05:00.750 --> 00:05:02.870
What do you think, Mr. Yanagida?

00:05:11.450 --> 00:05:13.290
Look at me.

00:05:14.660 --> 00:05:17.040
You're good at it, remember?

00:05:17.040 --> 00:05:19.700
Making me look amazing.

00:05:25.620 --> 00:05:26.660
It's showtime.

00:05:26.660 --> 00:05:27.910
What?

00:05:28.870 --> 00:05:29.910
Go!

00:05:34.160 --> 00:05:36.450
The show started.

00:05:36.450 --> 00:05:39.000
I go out in 13 minutes...

00:05:39.000 --> 00:05:40.620
Will you make it?

00:05:40.620 --> 00:05:42.120
Just now...

00:05:44.750 --> 00:05:48.870
Miss Fujito's hands were trembling...

00:05:48.870 --> 00:05:50.660
Of course they were.

00:05:50.660 --> 00:05:53.500
I'm not the only one who's been
forced into a corner...

00:05:54.790 --> 00:05:56.000
But...

00:05:57.370 --> 00:05:59.290
Gosh.

00:05:59.290 --> 00:06:04.040
You always put me on the spot, Miss Fujito.

00:06:08.750 --> 00:06:10.330
Thank you very much.

00:06:11.200 --> 00:06:13.410
I'm okay now.

00:06:13.410 --> 00:06:16.870
You can leave everything to me.

00:06:19.950 --> 00:06:21.660
Please stand still.

00:06:23.120 --> 00:06:24.870
The qualities of Miss Fujito...

00:06:24.870 --> 00:06:27.830
She has a great figure.

00:06:27.830 --> 00:06:34.250
When I saw her photo, her proportions
were no different than a runway model.

00:06:34.250 --> 00:06:39.370
She simply lacks the height.
Otherwise, she's well-proportioned.

00:06:40.750 --> 00:06:43.660
Another quality is her powerful presence.

00:06:43.660 --> 00:06:45.950
She emits a lot of energy.

00:06:45.950 --> 00:06:50.790
Because of her power,
she got me out of my head...

00:06:51.620 --> 00:06:53.950
Now on to the dress.

00:06:53.950 --> 00:06:57.620
It's designed to be an elegant form
that conceals the lines of the body...

00:06:57.620 --> 00:07:00.790
But in order to bring out
Miss Fujito's qualities,

00:07:00.790 --> 00:07:04.910
the dress needs texture
to match her youthful energy.

00:07:06.040 --> 00:07:10.370
I want to make a dress
that melts her tension away.

00:07:10.370 --> 00:07:12.290
Tsumura?

00:07:12.290 --> 00:07:14.040
All right. Please excuse me.

00:07:14.040 --> 00:07:15.160
What?

00:07:15.160 --> 00:07:16.620
--Hey! What are you doing, you idiot!

00:07:16.620 --> 00:07:18.000
--Ouch! Ouch!
--Hey! What are you doing, you idiot!

00:07:18.000 --> 00:07:21.290
We need to do something about the length!

00:07:21.290 --> 00:07:26.250
This dress has a cushion that functions
to create a unique shape.

00:07:26.250 --> 00:07:28.410
We need to take that out first.

00:07:28.410 --> 00:07:30.370
Don't worry. It's dark in here!

00:07:30.370 --> 00:07:31.700
I can't see anything!

00:07:31.700 --> 00:07:32.790
I really can't!

00:07:32.790 --> 00:07:33.950
Shut up!

00:07:33.950 --> 00:07:35.290
There's no time.

00:07:35.290 --> 00:07:37.080
Please just bear with me.

00:07:37.080 --> 00:07:41.950
He was so flustered seeing
naked bodies a second ago...

00:07:41.950 --> 00:07:44.450
Shoot. I hope I don't smell.

00:07:44.450 --> 00:07:46.000
I did just run over here...

00:07:46.000 --> 00:07:49.450
Miss Fujito, could you open your legs wider?

00:07:49.450 --> 00:07:51.700
Ouch! Ouch!

00:07:55.700 --> 00:07:57.700
I'm going to shorten it from here.

00:07:57.700 --> 00:07:59.330
What? So you are cutting it?

00:07:59.330 --> 00:08:01.120
Yes, I'm cutting it!

00:08:01.120 --> 00:08:03.700
If I can't process the hem...

00:08:03.700 --> 00:08:05.660
...I just have to make it disappear!

00:08:05.660 --> 00:08:07.160
So...

00:08:08.580 --> 00:08:09.750
He rolled it up.

00:08:09.750 --> 00:08:12.870
Now we use this belt!

00:08:12.870 --> 00:08:15.910
For the wearer, the back
is as important as the front.

00:08:16.540 --> 00:08:20.700
There's no way I could sew together
a bundle of thick fabric.

00:08:20.700 --> 00:08:22.250
That's why...

00:08:22.250 --> 00:08:23.750
...I'll tie it up!

00:08:26.080 --> 00:08:29.160
Bob! You've got five minutes!

00:08:29.160 --> 00:08:31.120
I need to make sure...

00:08:31.120 --> 00:08:33.330
...Miss Fujito walks on the runway!

00:08:35.870 --> 00:08:37.580
Please hang tight!

00:08:37.580 --> 00:08:40.540
I just need to finish this in time!

00:08:43.750 --> 00:08:44.950
Wow...

00:08:54.500 --> 00:08:55.790
Think!

00:08:55.790 --> 00:08:58.330
I don't have time to waste.

00:08:58.330 --> 00:09:00.790
The quality of the fabric,
the desired silhouette...

00:09:00.790 --> 00:09:03.450
No pattern... Not even a test run!

00:09:03.450 --> 00:09:05.620
I'll get it right all at once!

00:09:08.700 --> 00:09:09.950
Just a little more...

00:09:12.330 --> 00:09:13.700
Just a little more...

00:09:18.160 --> 00:09:19.580
Just a little more...

00:09:20.160 --> 00:09:21.580
Damn it!

00:09:25.750 --> 00:09:27.830
It's not ready yet, right?

00:09:27.830 --> 00:09:29.750
Don't worry.

00:09:29.750 --> 00:09:33.750
We could buy a little more time.

00:09:36.080 --> 00:09:39.370
The music is slower now.

00:09:39.370 --> 00:09:41.370
They're going for elegance.

00:09:41.370 --> 00:09:44.160
You can tell by the models' walks, too.

00:09:45.000 --> 00:09:46.500
You're right.

00:09:46.500 --> 00:09:48.750
They are walking slowly.

00:09:54.700 --> 00:09:59.250
Your dress kept changing every time
we came back from the runway.

00:09:59.250 --> 00:10:02.000
Everyone's excited.

00:10:03.410 --> 00:10:05.120
You can do this.

00:10:06.410 --> 00:10:07.540
Miss Fujito.

00:10:07.540 --> 00:10:08.950
Yeah?

00:10:08.950 --> 00:10:11.450
My dream I told you about...

00:10:11.450 --> 00:10:12.750
...it already came true.

00:10:12.750 --> 00:10:14.540
Huh? What do you mean?

00:10:14.540 --> 00:10:18.910
I wanted you to wear my clothes again.

00:10:18.910 --> 00:10:24.290
What are you talking about?
This doesn't count. It's not your brand.

00:10:25.750 --> 00:10:27.250
You better get on it.

00:10:27.250 --> 00:10:34.200
I might already be a hypermodel you can't hire
by the time you're starting up as a designer.

00:10:36.080 --> 00:10:38.830
You were trembling earlier--
that's quite the statement.

00:10:38.830 --> 00:10:40.250
What? You were watching me?

00:10:40.250 --> 00:10:42.410
More like... I felt it.

00:10:42.410 --> 00:10:44.500
Y-You're such a creep!

00:10:44.500 --> 00:10:47.870
Miss Fujito, please don't get nervous and fall.

00:10:47.870 --> 00:10:50.330
Who do you think I am?

00:10:50.330 --> 00:10:52.870
The model's coming back in ten seconds!

00:10:58.290 --> 00:11:00.200
All right Miss Fujito.

00:11:05.580 --> 00:11:07.250
Good luck.

00:11:10.790 --> 00:11:12.620
<i>Smile Down the Runway</i>.

00:11:18.200 --> 00:11:21.120
What? Are you bored, Niinuma?

00:11:21.120 --> 00:11:24.330
The models are all expressionless.

00:11:24.330 --> 00:11:27.120
This show is about showcasing the clothes.

00:11:27.120 --> 00:11:29.910
Bringing attention to their face
is not desirable.

00:11:29.910 --> 00:11:33.790
That's why models aren't allowed
to smile on the runway.

00:11:33.790 --> 00:11:36.950
It's an industry standard.
It looks better that way anyway.

00:11:38.500 --> 00:11:42.700
She's just pushing her values
and knowledge onto me...

00:11:42.700 --> 00:11:44.910
I know I won't look that amazing

00:11:44.910 --> 00:11:47.200
when I dress up anyway...

00:11:47.200 --> 00:11:50.040
Even if I dress up, nobody will notice.

00:11:50.040 --> 00:11:52.410
Nothing will look good

00:11:52.410 --> 00:11:54.410
on a shorty like me...

00:11:58.950 --> 00:12:01.370
What... is that?

00:12:01.370 --> 00:12:04.660
When you don't fit in,
you make a fool out of yourself.

00:12:04.660 --> 00:12:05.700
But...

00:12:05.700 --> 00:12:07.410
...even I...

00:12:11.290 --> 00:12:15.330
Even I've gone through a phase
where I was interested in fashion.

00:12:19.500 --> 00:12:22.950
Why is this tiny person

00:12:22.950 --> 00:12:24.750
walking for this show...?

00:12:28.950 --> 00:12:30.370
Huh? What is this?

00:12:30.370 --> 00:12:31.540
Is this a mishap?

00:12:31.540 --> 00:12:32.750
Looks that way.

00:12:32.750 --> 00:12:34.950
It has to be. Or else...

00:12:34.950 --> 00:12:38.370
There's no way a girl that short
could be on the runway!

00:12:40.580 --> 00:12:43.160
There's the commotion...

00:12:43.160 --> 00:12:45.040
It's just my imagination.

00:12:45.040 --> 00:12:47.620
I can't really hear anything.

00:12:47.620 --> 00:12:50.250
Everything in front of me is white.

00:12:50.250 --> 00:12:51.910
What I hear...

00:12:51.910 --> 00:12:53.950
...is the pounding of my heart

00:12:53.950 --> 00:12:56.160
and the faint music.

00:12:56.160 --> 00:12:58.500
I don't feel like myself at all.

00:12:58.500 --> 00:13:00.950
Was I the type to get this nervous?

00:13:01.950 --> 00:13:04.080
I can't afford to be nervous right now.

00:13:04.080 --> 00:13:05.370
Plus...

00:13:07.750 --> 00:13:09.700
I can't let Tsumura

00:13:09.700 --> 00:13:11.370
do better than me.

00:13:15.580 --> 00:13:18.250
Hey, Niinuma. Sit back down.

00:13:18.250 --> 00:13:20.290
Oh... I'm sorry...

00:13:20.290 --> 00:13:21.790
But that dress...

00:13:21.790 --> 00:13:24.580
It's made for that tiny model...

00:13:24.580 --> 00:13:25.950
What...?

00:13:25.950 --> 00:13:27.290
You're right.

00:13:27.290 --> 00:13:30.500
It seems like it was prepared for her.

00:13:30.500 --> 00:13:35.000
Maybe Hajime Yanagida wants to make

00:13:35.000 --> 00:13:37.410
a statement by using her as a model.

00:13:39.870 --> 00:13:41.620
Get ready for the finale.

00:13:41.620 --> 00:13:42.700
Yes!

00:13:47.950 --> 00:13:51.160
Hey! Why is #15 missing?

00:13:51.160 --> 00:13:54.830
I ordered you to choose from #1 to #12!

00:13:54.830 --> 00:13:58.540
But #15 was the smallest
and best fit for the model...

00:13:58.540 --> 00:14:02.580
Idiot! Those heels are broken!

00:14:05.000 --> 00:14:06.120
What?

00:14:06.120 --> 00:14:11.290
See? That's what you get for
trying to fit in where you don't.

00:14:11.290 --> 00:14:14.700
You fail, and everyone laughs at you...

00:14:15.580 --> 00:14:16.870
Amazing...

00:14:16.870 --> 00:14:17.910
Huh?

00:14:21.750 --> 00:14:23.370
Hey, Bob!

00:14:23.370 --> 00:14:24.950
Did you do that intentionally?

00:14:24.950 --> 00:14:26.790
Intentionally? No.

00:14:26.790 --> 00:14:29.700
I didn't assume she was going to fall.

00:14:29.700 --> 00:14:34.660
But there was so much tension,
I wanted to lighten things up.

00:14:34.660 --> 00:14:37.790
A shape-shifting dress sounded fun to me.

00:14:39.200 --> 00:14:42.750
That's why I didn't tie off that last thread.

00:14:48.500 --> 00:14:51.450
It's like the flutter of a butterfly.

00:14:51.450 --> 00:14:53.750
Everyone's looking at her...

00:14:53.750 --> 00:14:55.290
So it's okay...?

00:14:55.290 --> 00:14:58.040
To try to fit in where you don't?

00:14:58.040 --> 00:15:00.000
Then...

00:15:00.000 --> 00:15:01.950
Me, too...

00:15:01.950 --> 00:15:04.370
Shoot... I ruined it.

00:15:04.370 --> 00:15:06.250
But why?

00:15:06.250 --> 00:15:07.950
The heels gave out?

00:15:07.950 --> 00:15:12.450
It didn't come off, but it's pretty unstable.

00:15:12.450 --> 00:15:16.790
I'll have to change my walk
for the rest of the runway.

00:15:16.790 --> 00:15:17.750
It's okay.

00:15:17.750 --> 00:15:19.410
I got this.

00:15:19.410 --> 00:15:22.000
He just pulled a funny prank.

00:15:22.000 --> 00:15:24.500
Gosh... What a punk.

00:15:27.160 --> 00:15:31.950
He's just a coward who can't
do anything without my help.

00:15:34.870 --> 00:15:40.750
Chiyuki, as a runway model,
remember these two things.

00:15:40.750 --> 00:15:42.910
First and foremost, don't fall.

00:15:44.540 --> 00:15:46.200
Second...

00:15:49.330 --> 00:15:51.790
Never smile on the runway.

00:15:53.000 --> 00:15:56.500
The dress better look good
when she stands back up.

00:15:56.500 --> 00:15:58.950
Yes, it does. I put my all into it.

00:15:58.950 --> 00:16:02.000
Tsumura... You're so annoying.

00:16:03.160 --> 00:16:06.500
I don't know how you keep saving me.

00:16:08.700 --> 00:16:11.450
She smiled...

00:16:11.450 --> 00:16:12.870
...on the runway...

00:16:17.540 --> 00:16:19.370
Oh... What...?

00:16:19.370 --> 00:16:21.750
What's the matter?

00:16:21.750 --> 00:16:25.120
Is this okay...?

00:16:25.120 --> 00:16:27.830
She's tiny like me...

00:16:27.830 --> 00:16:31.370
She doesn't belong here, and yet...

00:16:32.750 --> 00:16:34.540
Of course it's okay.

00:16:37.950 --> 00:16:39.620
It's a huge success.

00:16:43.870 --> 00:16:46.000
Shoot! I got distracted.

00:16:46.000 --> 00:16:48.000
I smiled, too...

00:16:48.000 --> 00:16:49.410
Poker face!

00:16:56.160 --> 00:16:57.700
This reminds me

00:16:57.700 --> 00:17:05.870
of a writer who said they're not trying to
please the reader or deliver a message.

00:17:05.870 --> 00:17:10.160
It's about what you wish and want to be.

00:17:10.160 --> 00:17:13.450
It doesn't matter what others think.

00:17:13.450 --> 00:17:19.000
They do it to get closer to their ideal self.

00:17:19.000 --> 00:17:22.910
That's why they write.

00:17:22.910 --> 00:17:26.290
Why did I care so much about
what others thought?

00:17:26.290 --> 00:17:28.950
The same goes for fashion...

00:17:28.950 --> 00:17:31.950
It's something you make happen for yourself.

00:17:34.410 --> 00:17:37.700
Switch her heels out now!

00:17:37.700 --> 00:17:41.080
That's okay. I can keep going with these.

00:18:06.080 --> 00:18:07.120
Are you okay?

00:18:07.120 --> 00:18:09.750
Bring her some water and an ice pack.

00:18:09.750 --> 00:18:12.370
That was amazing! Great job!

00:18:13.830 --> 00:18:17.040
I only did two trips and my legs
are screaming at me.

00:18:18.120 --> 00:18:20.830
Huh? Where's Tsumura?

00:18:26.830 --> 00:18:28.200
Bear it!

00:18:28.200 --> 00:18:31.790
Bear the responsibility that this
show's success depends on you!

00:18:39.370 --> 00:18:42.290
I'll give you half.

00:18:42.290 --> 00:18:45.160
Half of this applause goes to you.

00:18:45.160 --> 00:18:46.160
What?

00:18:47.200 --> 00:18:50.950
This is my brand.
A split is the best I could do.

00:18:50.950 --> 00:18:52.200
You heard me.

00:18:52.200 --> 00:18:53.000
But I--

00:18:53.000 --> 00:18:55.580
Sure, your design was simple.

00:18:55.580 --> 00:19:00.700
You used an apron to cover up the portion
that was altered and lost its shape.

00:19:01.660 --> 00:19:06.450
But you still made it work.
The audience gave a standing ovation.

00:19:07.450 --> 00:19:12.040
Above all, you made the dress work
for the model, for her.

00:19:13.330 --> 00:19:19.080
Well there you go. You might have
a speck of potential as a designer.

00:19:22.660 --> 00:19:24.200
A designer...

00:19:28.290 --> 00:19:29.750
I-I'm sorry...

00:19:29.750 --> 00:19:32.830
I can't find my words right now...

00:19:36.080 --> 00:19:38.290
He's gone.

00:19:38.290 --> 00:19:39.830
Hey!

00:19:39.830 --> 00:19:42.700
Why aren't you showering me
with praise, Tsumura?

00:19:42.700 --> 00:19:46.080
Huh? I-I'm sorry. I was out of it...

00:19:46.080 --> 00:19:47.870
Gosh.

00:19:50.250 --> 00:19:53.950
Next time we're here,
let's take credit for all the applause.

00:19:53.950 --> 00:19:55.500
Not just half.

00:19:57.620 --> 00:20:00.700
You do know what I mean, right?

00:20:01.950 --> 00:20:03.540
Yes.

00:20:03.540 --> 00:20:06.040
Don't get too carried away now.

00:20:06.040 --> 00:20:06.910
Huh?

00:20:06.910 --> 00:20:12.080
First of all, you couldn't even
finish the fix on time.

00:20:12.080 --> 00:20:13.330
The tempo of the song,

00:20:13.330 --> 00:20:19.330
arrangement, and walking speed were
all carefully planned out for this show.

00:20:19.330 --> 00:20:23.000
Since it all went out the window,
the show wasn't at its best.

00:20:23.000 --> 00:20:25.290
But we still received a standing ovation.

00:20:25.290 --> 00:20:29.160
That's because of Mr. Hajime's
39 wonderful dresses.

00:20:29.160 --> 00:20:33.160
Not because of the dress you tailored.

00:20:33.160 --> 00:20:35.200
Don't get that confused.

00:20:36.410 --> 00:20:38.250
What's her problem?

00:20:38.250 --> 00:20:40.660
But she's right.

00:20:40.660 --> 00:20:47.370
My fixes were incomplete. The fabric around
the waist barely holds up its shape.

00:20:47.370 --> 00:20:54.120
If you didn't have your hand on your hip to hide it,
the awkward part would've been exposed.

00:20:57.700 --> 00:21:03.540
Miss Fujito, thank you very much
for making this happen for me.

00:21:03.540 --> 00:21:07.660
A lot happened and changed ever since we met...

00:21:07.660 --> 00:21:10.870
I feel like I'm living somebody else's life...

00:21:10.870 --> 00:21:15.200
I'm sorry, I can't find
the right words right now.

00:21:17.660 --> 00:21:20.200
Basically, you're saying that your life changed

00:21:20.200 --> 00:21:21.410
because of me, right?

00:21:21.410 --> 00:21:23.330
I-I think so...

00:21:23.330 --> 00:21:25.910
But it's embarrassing hearing you say that.

00:21:25.910 --> 00:21:27.450
What are you saying?

00:21:27.450 --> 00:21:32.540
My life changed because of you, too.

00:21:32.540 --> 00:21:35.660
We all wear clothes all the time, right?

00:21:35.660 --> 00:21:40.870
Clothes are with you even when
you're at crossroads in life.

00:21:41.910 --> 00:21:46.540
That's how special feelings
become attached to outfits.

00:21:46.540 --> 00:21:51.750
Clothes have the power
to transform someone's life.

00:21:51.750 --> 00:21:56.830
Niinuma, you wanted to be in
the literature division, right?

00:21:56.830 --> 00:22:00.000
Want me to put in a word
for you to the chief editor?

00:22:01.290 --> 00:22:04.120
I'm not saying we were perfect.

00:22:04.120 --> 00:22:07.790
That fitter was right, we had our flaws.

00:22:08.870 --> 00:22:10.540
But even then,

00:22:10.540 --> 00:22:13.200
we got that standing ovation.

00:22:13.200 --> 00:22:19.000
That means people were moved
by your dress and how I wore it.

00:22:19.000 --> 00:22:23.580
Who knows, we might've changed
someone else's life out there, too.

00:22:24.580 --> 00:22:30.540
No. I'd like to stay here and learn more.

00:22:42.040 --> 00:22:44.250
I want to become a designer.

00:22:45.250 --> 00:22:47.870
I'm going to be a designer.

00:22:49.450 --> 00:22:51.080
Damn it.

00:24:24.790 --> 00:24:29.160
There is a long and difficult road
for me to become a professional.

00:24:29.160 --> 00:24:31.120
But I'll never give up, no matter what!

00:24:31.120 --> 00:24:33.950
Next, "Young Talents."

00:24:33.950 --> 00:24:36.910
"See you next time!!"
